  "caption": "Quinn joined the work footy match, sprinted for the first time in ten years, and felt a twang. A week later it felt fine, so back to sprinting. Twang number two.\n\nHamstring strains often come back when people return too early, while there's still a strength gap at long, fast lengths. Stretching alone won't close that gap.\n\nWhat often helps: gentle holds early on, then gradually building slow-lowering, hip and trunk strength. Return to running in steps, with sprints last. Nordic curls can be a great addition: start with a small range and a few reps, and build over weeks.\n\nSevere pain, lots of bruising, a gap you can feel, or pain high near the sitting bone is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
